  (176, 'Clams are older than dinosaurs — some species are over 400 years old.'),
  (177, 'The entire Internet weighs about 50 grams — the weight of all the electrons in motion at any given moment.'),
  (178, 'In Japan, black cats are considered good luck rather than bad.'),
  (179, 'The speed of light is slightly faster than current law and technology allows the Internet to operate.'),
  (180, 'Broccoli, cabbage, kale, and Brussels sprouts are all the same species: Brassica oleracea.'),
  (181, 'The dot over the letter "i" and "j" is called a "tittle."'),
  (182, 'A full NASA spacesuit costs approximately $12 million — 70% of the cost is the backpack life support system.'),
  (183, 'Your nose and sinuses produce about a quart of mucus every day.'),
  (184, 'The Eiffel Tower was supposed to be demolished after 20 years but was saved because it was useful as a radio antenna.'),
  (185, 'Male lions sleep up to 22 hours a day.'),
  (186, 'There are 293 ways to make change for a US dollar.'),
  (187, 'A snail''s slime is so effective it can crawl over a razor blade without being cut.'),
