  (189, 'The original Ferris wheel, built in 1893, was 264 feet tall and could hold 2,160 passengers.'),
  (190, 'The world''s oldest piece of chewing gum is 5,000 years old, found in Finland.'),
  (191, 'In 1998, Sony accidentally sold 700,000 camcorders that could see through clothing in certain light conditions. They were all recalled.'),
  (192, 'The first product to have a barcode scanned was a pack of Wrigley''s chewing gum.'),
  (193, 'A polar bear''s liver contains so much Vitamin A that eating it would kill a human.'),
  (194, 'In 2019, a Dutch artist sold an "invisible" sculpture — literally nothing — for $18,000.'),
  (195, 'Cows produce more milk while listening to slow music. The best-performing song is reportedly "Everybody Hurts" by REM.'),
  (196, 'The most spoken language on Earth by number of people is Mandarin Chinese.'),
  (197, 'If you unraveled all the DNA in your body, it would stretch about 67 billion miles — far enough to reach the Sun and back 37 times.'),
  (198, 'There are more atoms in a grain of sand than grains of sand on all the world''s beaches.'),
  (199, 'The phrase "rule of thumb" comes from old English law, which allegedly permitted a husband to beat his wife with a stick no wider than his thumb.'),
  (200, 'Flamingos can only eat with their heads upside down.'),
  (201, 'The national animal of Australia (the kangaroo) and the emu were chosen partly because neither can walk backwards.'),
  (202, 'Cows can walk up stairs but not down them — their knees don''t bend the right way.'),
  (203, 'Iceland doesn''t have mosquitoes, reptiles, or squirrels — but it does have an Arctic fox.'),
  (204, 'The first YouTube video ever uploaded was titled "Me at the zoo," posted by co-founder Jawed Karim on April 23, 2005.'),
