  (206, 'A cubic mile of fog contains less than a gallon of water in droplet form.'),
  (207, 'Otters learn to swim from their mothers, often being carried on their back initially.'),
  (208, 'In Rome, it is illegal to feed the pigeons.'),
  (209, 'The entire population of the Earth could fit inside a cube with sides roughly 1 kilometer long.'),
  (210, 'The phrase "OK" is the most widely understood word on the planet.'),
  (211, 'Every continent''s name both starts and ends with the same letter.'),
  (212, 'Crows are capable of using tools — they can fashion hooks and probes from wire or sticks to extract food.'),
  (213, 'You can hear a blue whale''s heartbeat from two miles away.'),
  (214, 'Ketchup was used as medicine in the 1830s, prescribed for indigestion and liver complaints.'),
  (215, 'An elephant can smell water from up to 12 miles away.'),
  (216, 'Saturn is so light relative to its size that it would float in water.'),
  (217, 'Newborn elephants weigh about 260 pounds and can stand within minutes of birth.'),
  (218, 'A group of hippos is called a bloat.'),
  (219, 'The average American walks about 100,000 miles in their lifetime — about four times around the Earth.'),
  (220, 'It takes approximately 2 million flowers to make one pound of honey.'),
  (221, 'The number pi has been calculated to over 100 trillion decimal places and never repeats.'),
  (222, 'A duck''s quack doesn''t echo — and nobody knows why.'),
  (223, 'The first text message ever sent said "Merry Christmas" and was sent on December 3, 1992.'),
  (224, 'Goats were the first animals to be domesticated, roughly 10,000 years ago.'),
  (225, 'There are more possible nerve connections in one human brain than there are atoms in the universe.'),
  (226, 'The word "salary" shares its root with the word "salsa" — both derive from Latin "sal" (salt).'),
  (227, 'Chewing gum while peeling onions can prevent you from crying because it makes you breathe through your mouth.'),
  (228, 'A group of zebras is called a dazzle.'),
  (229, 'The average cloud is about the same weight as 80 elephants.'),
  (230, 'Newborn humans are the only mammals born completely helpless — most others can walk within hours.'),
  (231, 'A goldfish placed in a dark room will eventually lose its color.'),
  (232, 'Starlings in massive murmurations move so perfectly in sync that scientists still don''t fully understand how they do it.'),
  (233, 'The world''s first photograph took eight hours to expose — captured by Nicéphore Niépce in 1826.'),
  (234, 'Armadillos are the only non-human animals known to contract leprosy — and they frequently do.'),
  (235, 'A group of jellyfish is called a smack.'),
  (236, 'Crows have a region in their brain analogous to the human neocortex, which may explain their advanced problem-solving.'),
  (237, 'Farts travel at 10 feet per second (7 mph).'),
  (238, 'Japan has more vending machines per capita than any other country — about 1 for every 23 people.'),
  (239, 'The original Super Mario was designed by Miyamoto to minimize processing power — that''s why Mario has a mustache (no mouth to animate), a hat (no hair), and overalls (to show arm movement).'),
  (240, 'Cleopatra''s reign was closer to the Moon landing than to the construction of the pyramids by about 1,000 years.'),
  (241, 'The fingerprints of a koala are so similar to human fingerprints that they''ve been confused at crime scenes.'),
  (242, 'Cockroaches were around before the dinosaurs and will likely outlast most species on Earth.'),
  (243, 'The average lifespan of a taste bud is about 10 days.'),
  (244, 'A "moment" was once a precise unit of time — equal to 1.5 minutes in medieval manuscripts.'),
  (245, 'There are 86,400 seconds in a day, but also exactly 86,400 possible grid positions in a standard Sudoku puzzle.'),
  (246, 'Horses and cows sleep standing up but only reach deep REM sleep lying down.'),
  (247, 'The global population of chickens is about three times the total population of humans.'),
