  (416, 'There is a planet called 55 Cancri e where it may literally rain diamonds.'),
  (417, 'A crocodile cannot stick its tongue out.'),
  (418, 'There''s a 1-in-3 chance any given cloud you see will result in precipitation somewhere.'),
  (419, 'More than 50% of the world''s oxygen is produced by ocean phytoplankton.'),
  (420, 'Catfish have 27,000 taste buds — humans have only 10,000. Catfish can taste with their entire body.'),
  (421, 'The smell of rain has a name — "petrichor" — coined by scientists in 1964.'),
  (422, 'Wood frogs freeze solid in winter and thaw out in spring — their hearts stop and restart.'),
  (423, 'Only 5% of the ocean has been explored.'),
